  "id": "eval.2026-07-28-eval-164042.rag-ingestion-retrieval",
  "title": "RAG ingestion, retrieval, and grounded answers",
  "description": "# RAG ingestion, retrieval, and grounded answers\n\nThe board reads left to right across two main lanes. The top lane carries source arrivals and ACLs through normalization, content-hash classification, version-aware chunking, rate-limited embedding, and three-store version-consistent publication. The middle lane rewrites permission-bearing questions, performs parallel hybrid retrieval and reranking, filters evidence by the asking user’s access, and produces cited answers or an explicit “I don’t know.”\n\nFailure handling is embedded in the relevant stages: parse failures go to quarantine while batches continue; persistent embedding failures go to a dead-letter store; partial publication remains hidden until repaired or rolled back. Feedback records usefulness and unanswered questions and feeds coverage gaps back into ingestion priorities. The lower lane shows background re-embedding into a new generation, consistency validation, atomic promotion, and retention of the prior generation for rollback while live queries stay on the current generation.",
  "mode": "diagram",
